VENDORED THIRD-PARTY CODE
=========================
Each keeps its own license and attribution; do not strip per-file headers.

  - Sipeed / ZiyangYE RMII UDP stack ... rtl/vendor/sipeed_udp/
      Apache-2.0. RMII MAC + ARP + IPv4 + UDP engine for the RTL8201 PHY.
      Source: https://github.com/sipeed/TangPrimer-20K-example (Ethernet/verilog_UDP)
      Upstream author: ZiyangYE (https://github.com/ZiyangYE/Verilog_TCP)
      See its LICENSE + NOTICE.md.

  - nand2mario UART TX ................ rtl/vendor/nand2mario_ddr3/uart_tx_V2.v
      Apache-2.0. UART transmitter for the debug line.
      Source: https://github.com/nand2mario/ddr3-tang-primer-20k
      Upstream author: nand2mario.
      See its LICENSE + NOTICE.md.


GOWIN PROPRIETARY IP
====================
Gowin device-IP files are copyright Gowin Semiconductor and are NOT covered by
Groovy_Tang's GPL. They are either regenerated locally or vendored under Gowin's
own (proprietary) license; redistribution terms are Gowin's, not ours.

  - rtl/vendor/sipeed_udp/PLL_6M.v ...... Gowin rPLL IP (tracked; "IP file",
      Copyright Gowin Semiconductor). Came with the Sipeed UDP example.
  - rtl/board/.../video/dvi_tx/dvi_tx.v . Gowin DVI_TX IP. Proprietary/encrypted,
      git-ignored, regenerate locally (Gowin IP wizard) — see that dir's README.
  - rtl/board/.../gwddr3video/mem_pll.v . Gowin rPLL IP (tracked; "IP file").
  - rtl/board/.../gwddr3video/ddr3_ip/ .. Gowin DDR3 Memory Interface IP.
      Encrypted, git-ignored, regenerate locally — see that dir's README.

Gowin device primitives instantiated directly (rPLL, OSER, ELVDS_OBUF, B-SRAM,
DQS, etc.) are part of the toolchain/device and are not redistributed by us.


LICENSE COMPATIBILITY
=====================
The Apache-2.0 vendored blocks (Sipeed UDP, nand2mario UART) are incompatible
with GPLv2 but ARE compatible with GPLv3. Because Groovy_Tang is GPL-2.0-OR-LATER,
the combined/linked work may be used under GPLv3, under which Apache-2.0 is
compatible. Apache-2.0 NOTICE/attribution is preserved in each vendor directory.

The Gowin proprietary IP above is not GPL and not redistributed under our license;
it is used per Gowin's terms. Builds that include it are not redistributable as a
single GPL work — ship our GPL sources and let users regenerate the Gowin IP.


